        "The core 0455 requirement is the arithmetic of it: social cost = private cost + external cost; social benefit = private benefit + external benefit. State that first — it earns marks on its own.",
        "Negative externality of production (a polluting factory). Axes: price and quantity. The firm's supply curve is marginal PRIVATE cost, MPC. Marginal SOCIAL cost, MSC, lies ABOVE and to the LEFT of MPC, the vertical gap being the external cost per unit. Market output is where demand meets MPC (Q_market). The social optimum is where demand meets MSC (Q*), which is SMALLER. So the market OVER-produces, and the triangle between MSC, MPC and demand from Q* to Q_market is the welfare loss.",
